  "implementation_findings": [
    "The pinned SDK private dispatcher path must explicitly receive the configured read timeout; otherwise the controlled remote read-timeout test does not time out.",
    "The controlled Streamable HTTP timeout aborted the Client wait while the already-entered Tool coroutine completed, proving that timeout is not non-execution evidence.",
    "The SDK does not expose a general reliable not-dispatched proof after a remote timeout, so the application conservatively records POSSIBLY_SENT and POSSIBLY_EXECUTED.",
    "A trusted locally configured pre-handler contract can prove PROVEN_SENT plus PROVEN_NOT_EXECUTED; an unverified peer response body cannot.",
    "Authoritative NOT_EXECUTED is committed as a fact before the independent retry policy is consulted."
  ],
